  "query_preview": "..\nThe weather continues to remain quiet across the region, and this\nlooks to continue through Friday morning. Then, a disturbance along a\ntrough southwest of Wake Island may allow a low-level circulation to\ndevelop, with guidance indicating a potential tropical system of some\nsort (it may just be an Invest, or it may be something a little\nstronger),looks to pass through the far northern CNMI. As it\napproaches and crosses this region, a strengthening southwesterly\nwind may bring some breezy conditions along with scattered showers\nand maybe a thunderstorm or two to Tinian and Saipan, with the\nweather getting wetter the farther north you go.\n\nAs for Guam and Rota, isolated showers is all we can look for through\nthe weekend, especially with our nocturnal \"bump\" at night, when\nshower coverage is a little more. The tropical disturbance also may\nincrease winds some for Friday into the weekend, with breezy\nconditions possible for the higher terrain in southern Guam.\notherwise, the weather looks to remain fairly tame through the\nweekend.",
